At the request of ExI's Board of Directors, Pandit Singh has been expelled
from the Extropians email list.  He may not rejoin the list without the
permission of the Board.

The Board took this action in partial response to Singh's violation of
ExI's trademark in "Extropians."  Without having sought ExI's permission,
and with intent to misrepresent ExI's policies and goals, Singh set up a
newsgroup called "alt.extropians."  This alternative forum will confuse
potential consumers of ExI's goods and services by packaging un-Extropian
ideas under a name that ExI has reserved for its email list.  Singh has
thus intentionally infringed ExI's trademark, and ExI reserves the right to
levy additional moral and legal sanctions against him as it sees fit.

In expelling Singh, ExI's Board has exercised its plenary authority over
the Extropians email list.  The Board normally leaves regulation of the
list in the able hands of Harry Shapiro, the List Administrator.  But it
reserves the right to intervene in extraordinary circumstances, such as
this one, where ExI's vital interests are at stake. Harry thus effected
Singh's explusion in response to a direct request from ExI's Board, and
bears no responsibility for the Board's decision.


