Subject: META: suggestion for alt.extropians

  I agree with the posters who suggest that alt.extropians be
co-opted. I beleive it could be done to everyone's advantage.

We need a place to discuss the basic principles of extropianism, I
think. It is clearly stated that *this* list is not a place for that.
As a result, this list can get very one-sided, as extropian "true
believers" print long statements in response to non-conforming posts,
and which we are not allowed to publicly debate.
 
There are a lot of people like me on this list. I am fascinated with
the technology of futurism and not knowledgeable about the politics.
Other things, like uploading and cryonics, simply puzzle me. I would
still know nothing about cryonics if I had not met some extropians at
a party. On this list, I can get reading recommendations and read
essays, but cannot engage in questions-and-answers or the sort of
debate which I need to have to be convinced of a new idea.
  Personally, I was ready to leave the list until we started using
headers: now I kill certain topics, and consequently don't learn much.
How about a couple of volunteers coming over to alt.extropians and
debating the pros and cons of uploading with me? If it won't get us
kicked off of this list, that is. 

